.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt ERR_PRINT_ERRORS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ERR_print_errors ,
.Nm ERR_print_errors_fp ,
.Nm ERR_print_errors_cb
.Nd print error messages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/err.h
.Ft void
.Fo ERR_print_errors
.Fa "BIO *bp"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo ERR_print_errors_fp
.Fa "FILE *fp"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo ERR_print_errors_cb
.Fa "int (*cb)(const char *str"
.Fa "size_t len"
.Fa "void *u)"
.Fa "void *u"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn ERR_print_errors
is a convenience function that prints the error strings for all errors
that OpenSSL has recorded to
.Fa bp ,
thus emptying the error queue.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_print_errors_fp
is the same, except that the output goes to a
.Vt FILE .
.Pp
.Fn ERR_print_errors_cb
is the same, except that the callback function,
.Sy cb ,
is called for each error line with the string, length, and userdata
.Fa u
as the callback parameters.
.Pp
The error strings will have the following format:
.Bd -literal
 [pid]:error:[error code]:[library name]:[function name]:[reason string]:[filename]:[line]:[optional text message]
.Ed
.Pp
.Em error code
is an 8 digit hexadecimal number.
.Em library name ,
.Em function name
and
.Em reason string
are ASCII text, as is
.Em optional text message
if one was set for the respective error code.
.Pp
If there is no text string registered for the given error code, the
error string will contain the numeric code.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn ERR_print_errors
and
.Fn ERR_print_errors_fp
return no values.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_error_string 3 ,
.Xr ERR_get_error 3
